# FlightMate Project Context

Before making any change, read `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` at the repository root.
It defines what FlightMate is (and is not), its architecture, and its
coding rules. Treat it as the source of truth for scope and conventions.

## What FlightMate is

A native macOS companion for Aerofly FS 4: live UDP telemetry + AI-powered
contextual assistance to help users learn aviation and improve their
flight simulation experience (dashboard, AI instructor, flight phase
detection, aircraft-specific checklists, airport info, flight history).

## What FlightMate is NOT

Not a flight simulator, ATC replacement, moving map clone, weather
injector, autopilot, or plugin. Do not build features that drift toward
these.

## Architecture

SwiftUI, MVVM, `Network.framework`, SwiftData, feature-first architecture,
dependency injection.

## Coding rules (non-negotiable)

- Never use UIKit.
- Never use singletons — inject dependencies via initializers.
- Never hardcode airport data.
- Keep files under 300 lines; split when a file grows past this.
- Every service must be testable (protocol-oriented / constructor-injected
  dependencies, no hidden global state).
- Prefer protocol-oriented design over concrete-type coupling.
- UI (Views) must not contain business logic — that belongs in
  ViewModels/Services in `Core/`.
